# eOn SVN r2549. HarnessCounter through ext_pot. Kernel lammps.
# Climbing-image NEB, same stops as eon/develop-de-lj38-cap. Five images, L-BFGS memory 20, max_move 0.05, max_iterations 8000, converged_force 0.001. The harness cap is 2500. Potential lammps, the archived in.lammps lj/cut kernel. Main random_seed is 1. r2549 does not read energy_weighted, ci_mmf, climbing_image_band_slack, setup_mmf_peaks, or the develop L-BFGS catalog past memory, inverse curvature, max inverse curvature, auto scale, and the two resets. Those keys are omitted. The keys it does read sit in [Optimizer]. The run swaps the potential for ext_pot. The harness kernel is the develop kernel for this potential name. The 2014 table used r2156. The binary is SVN r2549, the registry pin. Export of the 2014 revision is forbidden, so this row is r2549.
